WEBVTT

00:35.010 --> 00:39.980
"Censorship"

00:39.020 --> 00:47.990
The inspection and control of the printed word

00:39.020 --> 00:47.990
or speech deemed to be improper by the state.

00:47.110 --> 00:53.990
It is forbidden by Article 21 of the Japanese Constitution.

00:53.070 --> 00:58.330
Libraries, the last bastion against such suppression,

00:57.870 --> 01:02.830
formed the Library Defense Force to protect free speech.

01:02.380 --> 01:09.420
Its battle with the Media Betterment Committee continues.

01:19.770 --> 01:23.810
We're now conducting an inspection under
Article 3 of the MBA.

01:46.590 --> 01:48.340
<i>The Media Betterment Act.</i>

01:48.800 --> 01:56.510
<i>Enacted to regulate expression violating order and morality as we entered the Seika Period.</i>

01:57.890 --> 02:01.680
<i>Much is unclear about how it came into being.</i>

02:01.680 --> 02:05.230
<i>Many call it unconstitutional.</i>

02:04.270 --> 02:09.690
Year 34 of the Seika Period

02:13.740 --> 02:16.450
What am I going to do?!

02:13.780 --> 02:16.450
Kantou Book Station Dormitory

02:20.410 --> 02:24.210
Hey, Shibasaki! Could you take a look?

02:24.370 --> 02:26.040
I'm busy.

02:26.040 --> 02:29.340
Don't say that, help me out!

02:29.960 --> 02:33.550
Don't get so worked up over a date.

02:34.630 --> 02:36.010
Worked up?!

02:36.470 --> 02:40.930
It's not a date, there's something I've got to do.

02:41.350 --> 02:44.140
You're going to drink chamomile tea.

02:44.140 --> 02:46.400
That sounds like a date to me.

02:47.060 --> 02:50.320
Why else would you worry about clothes?

02:50.820 --> 02:54.530
I just... uh... don't want to be rude!

02:54.530 --> 03:00.410
You were <i>plenty</i> rude to him when he was your instructor.

03:03.870 --> 03:06.620
If you're going to a cafe, wear jeans.

03:07.750 --> 03:13.510
Plus aren't those layered camisole and
sweater and sky blue down jacket fine?

03:14.880 --> 03:18.850
Armed Terrorist Attack!?

03:15.550 --> 03:18.850
You'll look classy without overdoing it.

03:19.550 --> 03:22.100
Thanks, Shibasaki!

03:22.100 --> 03:28.020
In return, could you tell Admin I'm sick? Say it's just a cold.

03:28.020 --> 03:32.650
No way! You can't take sick leave just to watch the news!

03:32.650 --> 03:34.820
But this is a major incident!

03:34.820 --> 03:38.530
My instincts are telling me to keep watching.

03:38.530 --> 03:41.370
There's <i>no</i> way I'm letting you!

04:02.970 --> 04:05.810
The Wings of Revolution

04:06.600 --> 04:09.480
Library Officer 2nd Class/Library Task Force member . Dojo Squad Captain

04:08.730 --> 04:09.480
Short but Feisty

04:09.940 --> 04:13.530
Library Officer 2nd Class/Library Task Force member . Dojo Squad Vice-captain

04:12.020 --> 04:13.530
Logical Funnyman

04:13.820 --> 04:17.110
Chief Librarian/Library Task Force member . Dojo Squad member

04:15.940 --> 04:17.110
Young and Stubborn

04:17.400 --> 04:20.950
Chief Librarian/Musashino No 1 Library . Library Administration member

04:19.490 --> 04:20.950
Info-Savvy

04:43.640 --> 04:47.020
Library Supervisor First Class . Library Task Force Captain

04:45.770 --> 04:47.020
Middle-Aged Brawler

05:05.450 --> 05:10.040
Chief Librarian/Library Task Force member . Dojo Squad member

05:07.580 --> 05:10.040
Passionate but Awkward

05:33.150 --> 05:38.740
Today at 3 am, at the Tsuruga nuclear plant in Fukui,

05:38.740 --> 05:42.320
a military helicopter crashed into reactors 3 and 4.

05:42.990 --> 05:48.910
Armed terrorists who were on board attacked the plant, opening fire

05:48.910 --> 05:59.090
Material Source              .      Police Department

05:48.910 --> 05:52.080
<i>on police and the Self-Defense Force,</i>

05:52.080 --> 05:55.380
<i>but the reactor cores were shut down,</i>

05:55.380 --> 05:59.090
<i>and no radiation leaks have been detected.</i>

05:59.420 --> 06:02.800
Residents of northern Tsuruga may now return to their homes...

06:06.180 --> 06:07.850
Apologies for being late, sir!

06:08.770 --> 06:12.560
Don't salute in civvy clothes! People will look!

06:15.360 --> 06:16.860
I'm sorry!

06:19.860 --> 06:21.240
Since you...

06:25.030 --> 06:27.700
Since you dressed so nicely, don't run.

06:34.870 --> 06:36.460
How about lunch today?

06:36.460 --> 06:37.630
Well...

06:41.210 --> 06:43.220
So this is chamomile tea.

06:45.720 --> 06:46.930
What?

06:46.930 --> 06:50.430
I didn't expect you to order cake!

06:51.140 --> 06:53.060
Got a problem with that?

06:53.060 --> 06:56.190
No! I think it's cute.

06:56.520 --> 06:59.320
Well, your face looks different from usual.

06:59.320 --> 07:01.320
Huh? In what way?

07:01.320 --> 07:02.650
More feminine.

07:04.780 --> 07:08.200
I'm not on duty, so can't I even wear some make-up?!

07:08.530 --> 07:10.240
I didn't put much on, though.

07:11.080 --> 07:14.410
Does it look weird? Do I look weird?!

07:14.410 --> 07:18.920
Nobody said you looked weird. Just different than usual.

07:19.750 --> 07:23.720
Library Canteen

07:28.640 --> 07:30.260
A nuke plant attack...

07:31.350 --> 07:33.140
Tezuka, aren't you off the clock today?

07:33.770 --> 07:35.770
I got bored in my room.

07:36.060 --> 07:39.810
I thought you might be gawking at the TV here,

07:39.810 --> 07:41.110
and I was right.

07:41.570 --> 07:42.730
Give me a break.

07:43.440 --> 07:46.280
Information gathering is my duty.

07:46.700 --> 07:50.160
But this has nothing to do with libraries.

07:50.160 --> 07:53.830
All terrorists found dead

07:51.240 --> 07:55.290
I really hope that it doesn't.

07:55.960 --> 07:57.040
Why is that?

07:57.040 --> 07:59.250
All terrorists found dead

07:57.370 --> 07:58.960
It's private.

07:59.250 --> 08:03.090
All terrorists found dead

08:00.500 --> 08:03.090
If I told you, I'd jinx it.

08:03.500 --> 08:06.630
I believe in that kind of stuff.

08:18.940 --> 08:20.650
What a cute looking cup.

08:22.110 --> 08:23.440
Nice design, I guess.

08:28.660 --> 08:33.580
You first showed me a chamomile flower
on duty during the Ibaraki exhibition.

08:33.830 --> 08:37.660
Oh, Captain Genda will be transferring here soon.

08:40.170 --> 08:43.170
He shielded the exhibits with his body

08:43.170 --> 08:46.090
and got shot 32 times in return.

08:46.090 --> 08:49.510
He heals crazily fast for an old geezer.

08:49.510 --> 08:51.760
How can you call him that?

08:52.390 --> 08:54.970
It's just between the two of us.

08:56.980 --> 08:58.850
<i>"Between the two of us..."</i>

09:00.520 --> 09:01.350
What should we do after this?

09:03.570 --> 09:05.480
Wanna go see a movie?

09:06.320 --> 09:10.860
<i>This is turning into something a lot like a normal date!</i>

09:20.830 --> 09:21.880
Hello?             Hello?

09:21.880 --> 09:23.920
Sorry to call mid-date.

09:23.920 --> 09:25.000
It's no date!          It's no date!

09:25.710 --> 09:28.380
So you're hitting it off as usual.

09:28.800 --> 09:32.470
Anyway, Instructor Komaki wants to talk.

09:33.300 --> 09:38.430
I'm really sorry, but we need you here.
It's an emergency.

09:38.980 --> 09:40.560
An emergency?!              An emergency?!

09:47.440 --> 09:48.860
We'll keep watch.

09:50.110 --> 09:52.530
MBC agents?

09:52.530 --> 09:53.820
No doubt.

09:55.160 --> 09:56.080
We're going in!

10:04.170 --> 10:06.170
Dojo and Kasahara reporting back!

10:10.880 --> 10:13.930
Nice to see you two are so friendly.

10:16.010 --> 10:16.930
This is...

10:17.510 --> 10:19.220
...because she's slow!

10:19.430 --> 10:22.770
Everyone knows Kasahara's a fast runner.

10:26.610 --> 10:28.780
What's going on exactly?

10:29.650 --> 10:32.400
Ms. Orikuchi from the Sesousha will explain.

10:35.780 --> 10:36.870
Are you okay?

10:37.780 --> 10:39.330
I-I'm sorry!

10:39.950 --> 10:42.460
Ms. Orikuchi, who's this?

10:42.790 --> 10:44.290
Touma Kurato...

10:45.080 --> 10:46.170
Sir!

10:46.170 --> 10:47.540
The author?!

10:48.040 --> 10:48.960
Yes.

10:49.920 --> 10:54.260
I've come to ask you to assign him a personal bodyguard.

10:54.470 --> 10:56.720
I'm truly sorry.

10:56.720 --> 10:58.970
A personal bodyguard?

10:58.970 --> 11:04.730
Ryoujitsu Newspaper

10:58.970 --> 11:04.730
Nuclear Terror Incident

10:58.970 --> 11:04.730
Terrorists dead

10:58.970 --> 11:04.730
No leakage of

10:58.970 --> 11:04.730
Radiation

11:00.140 --> 11:04.140
I believe you've all heard about the terrorist attack?

11:05.100 --> 11:11.570
An anti-terrorism bill was passed this morning giving agencies more jurisdiction,

11:11.570 --> 11:14.820
including the Media Betterment Committee.

11:15.740 --> 11:20.450
A law giving more jurisdiction to the MBC?

11:20.450 --> 11:21.950
What's going on?

11:23.580 --> 11:25.830
It's regarding "Nuclear Peril", isn't it?

11:26.880 --> 11:33.840
Nuclear Peril

11:26.880 --> 11:33.840
Media Publication

11:28.460 --> 11:33.510
The terrorists' actions mirror those depicted in this novel.

11:34.220 --> 11:41.010
So, Mr. Touma's under suspicion because they seem to be using his novel as a textbook.

11:41.680 --> 11:44.520
Touma

11:42.060 --> 11:44.520
But isn't that a coincidence?

11:45.100 --> 11:48.520
It doesn't matter if it is or not.

11:48.980 --> 11:56.990
The Media Betterment Committee might use this to put pressure on Mr. Touma, correct?

11:57.660 --> 12:03.910
Word is they'll try to arrest him and take away his right to write.

12:04.620 --> 12:08.120
This time it's not just books,

12:08.120 --> 12:12.380
they'll use this to crack down on authors as well.

12:12.800 --> 12:15.050
If they succeed,

12:15.050 --> 12:20.090
Mr. Touma will be the first casualty of a war on writers.

12:20.550 --> 12:22.060
A war on writers?

12:23.310 --> 12:24.310
Excuse me!

12:25.600 --> 12:27.690
What should I do?

12:27.690 --> 12:29.150
No need to worry!

12:30.400 --> 12:32.900
We will definitely protect you.

12:35.070 --> 12:44.990
We're preparing to indict the MBC for violating the constitutional right for free speech, with Mr. Touma as plaintiff.

12:45.910 --> 12:47.710
A court case?

12:48.040 --> 12:52.380
It could drag on as far as the Supreme Court.

12:52.380 --> 12:55.920
We'll protect Mr. Touma until he's cleared.

12:56.170 --> 12:59.050
The MBC must never capture him. Got it?

13:04.600 --> 13:05.970
Disguises?

13:06.220 --> 13:10.690
The MBC are still unaware that Mr. Touma's with us.

13:11.020 --> 13:15.230
They'll find out eventually, but it'll buy us time.

13:15.570 --> 13:18.700
His face is definitely well-known.

13:19.150 --> 13:21.780
He'll be convincing as one of us.

13:21.780 --> 13:25.790
So, can you two buy some regular old guy eyeglasses,

13:25.990 --> 13:28.410
and some black hair dye?

13:28.620 --> 13:32.630
But why are you putting us together again?

13:32.790 --> 13:36.000
Well, you're already in plain clothes.

13:36.000 --> 13:37.840
So buy some fake specs.

13:37.840 --> 13:45.560
Let's be

13:37.840 --> 13:45.560
arranged
& ordered

13:37.840 --> 13:43.760
Act like lovers out shopping, and the MBC will never notice you.

13:43.760 --> 13:45.560
Lovers? As if...

13:47.770 --> 13:49.520
How about these?

13:50.310 --> 13:52.650
These are the lenses I want.

13:55.520 --> 13:59.190
I just ordered them. It'll take a while though.

13:59.820 --> 14:01.320
Do you like these?

14:01.780 --> 14:04.120
For you. Aren't you buying too?

14:08.040 --> 14:08.790
Yes.

14:11.830 --> 14:16.340
They're not bad at all. You almost look intelligent.

14:16.340 --> 14:18.250
What do you mean, almost?!

14:19.170 --> 14:20.170
They're on me.

14:20.170 --> 14:23.010
I wanted some, so I'll buy them myself!

14:23.760 --> 14:25.260
But I...

14:37.440 --> 14:40.320
Do we really have to go this far?

14:40.900 --> 14:44.030
I'm sorry, it's for your own safety.

14:45.490 --> 14:47.490
I liked my old hairstyle.

14:51.330 --> 14:53.540
I've guarded books before,

14:54.040 --> 14:57.000
but never an author.

14:57.380 --> 15:01.380
They extended the reach of the Media Betterment Act.

15:01.380 --> 15:05.970
We can only do the same with the Library Freedom Law.

15:05.970 --> 15:11.220
But that'll only increase the scale of the battle.

15:12.350 --> 15:12.930
Kasahara?

15:13.940 --> 15:14.980
Yes?

15:16.560 --> 15:17.610
For you.

15:19.020 --> 15:21.070
An eyeglass case?

15:21.570 --> 15:23.740
It's like that cup, right?

15:24.490 --> 15:26.570
The one you said was cute.

15:36.040 --> 15:37.420
I'm happy!

15:37.880 --> 15:39.540
Thank you!

15:40.460 --> 15:41.880
Dojo?

15:44.590 --> 15:45.430
Ms. Kojima?

15:46.510 --> 15:47.640
Long time!

15:48.300 --> 15:49.640
Still in the LDF?

15:49.640 --> 15:50.760
Yes.

15:51.640 --> 15:55.270
You must rank a lot higher than you did then.

15:55.270 --> 15:56.770
Well, I'm...

15:59.520 --> 16:02.110
No good? Still not ready?

16:09.870 --> 16:11.200
I work here now.

16:11.200 --> 16:11.700
Kinokuniya Book Store

16:11.200 --> 16:11.700
Chief Clerk          Kojima Sayaka

16:13.700 --> 16:17.620
If I can ever help you with anything, let me know.

16:18.000 --> 16:21.090
I still owe you one.

16:21.790 --> 16:23.050
No, that's...

16:23.380 --> 16:28.760
I'll never forget what you did for me back then.

16:32.350 --> 16:35.730
Oh no! I've got to go.

16:35.730 --> 16:36.810
Oh.

16:37.390 --> 16:40.770
I'll drop by the library. Bye now!

16:44.480 --> 16:46.900
Come on, let's head back.

16:46.900 --> 16:47.950
Uh, okay!

16:54.910 --> 16:59.710
Author Touma Kurato is banned from writing.

16:56.120 --> 16:57.620
Nuclear Peril

16:58.120 --> 17:02.130
Censored publication                Nuclear Peril

16:59.710 --> 17:02.130
While he is wanted by the Media Betterment Committee,

17:02.130 --> 17:05.420
we know that he is in Library Defense Force custody.

17:02.630 --> 17:06.090
Author    .     Touma Kurato           (59)

17:06.260 --> 17:11.430
The LDF plan to indict the MBC with Touma as plaintiff

17:09.550 --> 17:13.010
Court

17:11.430 --> 17:15.850
on the grounds that their actions are unconstitutional.

17:27.110 --> 17:29.820
Nuclear Peril

17:27.110 --> 17:29.820
Media Publication

17:28.700 --> 17:33.450
Ms. Orikuchi, if I may speak hypothetically...

17:33.450 --> 17:34.280
Of course.

17:34.620 --> 17:39.000
If, and I mean if, we were to negotiate with the MBC,

17:39.370 --> 17:43.670
and had "Nuclear Peril" removed from bookstores,

17:43.670 --> 17:48.090
do you think I would be able to walk free?

17:48.340 --> 17:53.550
Without the ability to write, I'm worthless.

17:54.140 --> 17:58.020
The MBC have already made their position clear...

17:58.810 --> 18:00.690
So it's a no-go!

18:10.900 --> 18:15.950
I'm here to see Dojo Atsushi. My name is Kojima Sayaka.

18:15.950 --> 18:18.750
I'll call him. Please have a seat.

18:28.550 --> 18:33.840
Sorry to turn up suddenly. We didn't have time to talk before.

18:34.140 --> 18:37.600
If you'd asked, I would've come to see you.

18:37.890 --> 18:41.060
Work must be hectic for you lately.

18:41.520 --> 18:45.270
I saw a lot of MBC agents on my way here.

18:45.650 --> 18:48.270
We do have something on right now.

18:48.780 --> 18:51.820
You're a fan of Mr. Touma, aren't you?

18:51.820 --> 18:56.280
I'm just doing what I can. Business as usual.

18:59.200 --> 19:04.710
Maybe it was business as usual for you, but it was special for me.

19:18.890 --> 19:20.100
I'm home!

19:20.470 --> 19:21.810
Hi!

19:22.680 --> 19:28.650
Hey, the Tokyo District Court ruling's tomorrow. I wonder what it'll be?

19:29.820 --> 19:35.570
Touma's got the LDF and his publisher backing him up, so he can't lose.

19:36.740 --> 19:38.320
You know, right?

19:38.320 --> 19:38.990
What?

19:39.330 --> 19:44.500
That a woman came to talk with Instructor Dojo today.

19:44.500 --> 19:45.370
You know, right?

19:46.330 --> 19:48.080
Oh, I see!

19:48.920 --> 19:51.300
Cut the act!

19:51.300 --> 19:54.800
You're obviously trying to hide your shock.

19:54.800 --> 19:57.140
I'm not shocked!

19:57.140 --> 19:59.680
But I knew about the woman.

20:00.180 --> 20:02.680
She was quite pretty.

20:02.680 --> 20:06.690
And most of all, she was shorter than Dojo.

20:08.270 --> 20:11.360
Why don't you ask him how he feels?

20:11.360 --> 20:16.030
Then you won't have to worry whether you're dating or not.

20:16.530 --> 20:17.860
Thanks.

20:18.240 --> 20:19.490
But it's okay.

20:20.120 --> 20:22.290
What's okay?

20:22.290 --> 20:25.790
I came here because I wanted to be a prince.

20:26.920 --> 20:29.080
Just like Instructor Dojo.

20:29.500 --> 20:33.960
So I've spent the last 3 years trying to impress him.

20:34.880 --> 20:40.850
I think he's kind to me because he recognizes the effort I've put in.

20:41.430 --> 20:49.150
It's his way of praising my dedication as an LDF member, and as a task force member.

20:50.730 --> 20:52.150
For me...

20:53.020 --> 20:55.070
that's enough.

21:02.450 --> 21:03.740
Instructor Dojo!

21:05.370 --> 21:06.540
What is it?

21:06.910 --> 21:08.750
I'll get chamomile too!

21:09.330 --> 21:10.580
Chamomile?

21:11.630 --> 21:15.260
I want the same chamomile rank as you, sir!

21:18.930 --> 21:20.090
Do your best.

21:20.680 --> 21:22.720
But why all this now?

21:23.050 --> 21:24.810
I'll definitely get it!

21:39.950 --> 21:47.160
Contemplating Free Expression and Censorship

21:40.280 --> 21:43.580
And now, Library Future Plan Committee chairman

21:43.580 --> 21:47.160
Tezuka Satoshi with a few words.

21:47.160 --> 21:52.130
Contemplating Free Expression and Censorship

21:53.210 --> 21:56.920
It is my great honor to speak in front of

21:56.920 --> 22:02.340
so many Diet members and other
esteemed guests gathered here today.

22:02.340 --> 22:06.850
In combating censorship, the LDF is not effective.

22:06.850 --> 22:09.770
On the contrary, it is obstructive.

22:09.770 --> 22:13.980
What is truly needed is legal and systemic reform.

22:10.310 --> 22:16.270
Contemplating Free Expression and Censorship

22:16.860 --> 22:21.990
Today, the Tokyo District Court ruled in favor of Touma Kurato

22:22.700 --> 22:29.200
and deemed the Media Betterment
Committee's actions to be unconstitutional.

22:30.000 --> 22:33.170
The MBC immediately filed an appeal.

22:47.510 --> 22:49.930
Mr. Touma, things have changed.

22:50.600 --> 22:53.480
It's late, but please come with us.

23:06.870 --> 23:10.330
I'm dying to know how have things changed.

23:10.910 --> 23:13.210
You don't have to answer now.

23:13.620 --> 23:16.750
You'll tell a court of inquiry though.

23:16.750 --> 23:18.040
Watch your back!

23:18.380 --> 23:20.760
You too, Mr. Tezuka's brother!

23:22.090 --> 23:23.470
You're his men?!

23:24.050 --> 23:28.430
I pity you for being unable to understand his ideals!

23:29.350 --> 23:32.270
You don't know anything! Shut up!

23:32.270 --> 23:33.640
Enough, Tezuka.

23:37.980 --> 23:40.320
Library Future Plan agents.

23:41.480 --> 23:44.820
You were right to switch Mr. Touma's room.

23:44.820 --> 23:48.490
But I never imagined an attack by LDF members.

23:50.540 --> 23:53.790
I despise Tezuka's older brother.

23:54.830 --> 23:58.500
Tezuka won't hate him despite his betrayals.

23:59.250 --> 24:02.920
And his brother uses that, again and again!

24:07.300 --> 24:08.850
I want to be alone.

24:09.800 --> 24:14.430
You just don't want people to know you're vulnerable.

24:22.320 --> 24:23.610
W-Why?

24:24.860 --> 24:27.740
It was shock therapy.

24:27.780 --> 24:29.280
Shock therapy?!

24:29.910 --> 24:33.040
I thought I should do that sometime

24:33.040 --> 24:35.370
to a guy who's not anybody.

24:36.460 --> 24:38.290
Sorry if it was unwanted.

24:38.790 --> 24:42.000
Just view it as a passing whim.

24:42.000 --> 24:43.630
A whim?!

24:43.920 --> 24:47.880
I don't... think you're... nobody.

24:48.430 --> 24:51.970
Then I need a favor as collateral.

24:53.180 --> 24:55.930
Switch phones with me for a while.

24:56.980 --> 25:00.480
Are you serious?! Why should I switch...

25:05.990 --> 25:07.650
I need it right now.

25:08.150 --> 25:12.030
There's someone I can only call with your phone.

25:13.870 --> 25:17.620
Are you planning to take on my brother?

25:20.880 --> 25:21.790
Alright.

25:21.790 --> 25:22.590
Huh?!

25:22.590 --> 25:23.800
But I need collateral.

25:32.140 --> 25:38.480
The Media Betterment Act appeal trial began in the Tokyo High Court today.

25:38.890 --> 25:46.190
How will it view the District Court's ruling against the MBC?

25:46.900 --> 25:56.660
The LDF base is no longer safe. So Mr. Touma is now under guard at the home of former base commander Inamine.

26:06.170 --> 26:08.840
I hope you can be at ease here.

26:09.220 --> 26:12.590
This garden was my late wife's pastime.

26:12.590 --> 26:17.810
Now I let others to tend to it, but I try to keep it as it was.

26:18.640 --> 26:23.060
I'd be happy to help with your garden at any time.

26:23.060 --> 26:27.400
Your height would certainly come in handy.

26:27.400 --> 26:33.070
Don't let her near your garden,
unless you want to see it destroyed.

26:33.070 --> 26:34.410
How dare you!

26:34.660 --> 26:38.040
I'll have you know my parents are farmers!

26:38.040 --> 26:40.580
Farming isn't like gardening!

26:40.580 --> 26:44.420
You want to turn this garden into a potato field?!

26:45.750 --> 26:48.760
So you're an expert on gardening now?!

26:54.300 --> 26:56.760
Feel free to use anything here.

26:57.180 --> 27:00.730
I hope it will be of help for your writing.

27:01.390 --> 27:04.440
That's not going to be easy right now.

27:10.530 --> 27:13.490
The Hino's Nightmare: A Complete Record

27:14.780 --> 27:16.780
Let's eat!

27:20.660 --> 27:21.750
Delicious!

27:22.120 --> 27:24.120
Mrs. Fuku sure can cook!

27:24.120 --> 27:25.960
She's a great help to me.

27:27.790 --> 27:30.510
This soy sauce stew is superb.

27:30.510 --> 27:35.050
Mr. Instructor, craving a beer perhaps? I'll buy some.

27:35.050 --> 27:37.550
N-not while we're on duty!

27:37.850 --> 27:39.810
Don't be so uptight.

27:39.810 --> 27:43.730
You idiot! You'll make us look unprofessional!

27:45.730 --> 27:46.480
Excuse me!

27:46.810 --> 27:48.150
Yes?

27:48.400 --> 27:50.150
Is there any mayonnaise?

27:50.150 --> 27:52.280
Uh, I'll go get some.

27:52.280 --> 27:57.950
I'm sorry, we don't have any. I don't use it.

27:59.030 --> 28:00.660
Soy sauce is fine.

28:00.660 --> 28:01.790
Sauce, sure.

28:04.370 --> 28:06.120
You idiot!

28:06.120 --> 28:07.670
I-I'm so sorry!

28:07.670 --> 28:10.170
Gondo Tempura Restaurant

28:11.420 --> 28:13.130
Your fiddleheads.

28:13.380 --> 28:16.340
Even if you truly weren't aware of it,

28:16.340 --> 28:24.520
the attempted abduction of Touma is a perfect excuse to purge Library Future Plan members from the LDF.

28:24.520 --> 28:28.520
I thought that's why I'm treating you to dinner.

28:28.980 --> 28:33.400
You know you can't solve this problem that easily.

28:33.400 --> 28:39.950
So, I'd like to use my unassailable position to present you with a proposal.

28:39.950 --> 28:41.160
I'm listening.

28:43.410 --> 28:45.460
This is delicious!

28:47.370 --> 28:50.000
To create a censorship-free society!

28:50.000 --> 28:54.380
That's our mutual end objective, am I correct?

28:54.760 --> 29:00.350
I believe that censorship and the MBF who enforce it are unjust.

29:00.350 --> 29:05.560
Censorship only exists to protect the interests of a select few.

29:05.930 --> 29:06.890
Indeed.

29:07.440 --> 29:12.110
However, that doesn't mean that you and the LDF are just.

29:12.110 --> 29:13.900
Do you understand that?

29:14.570 --> 29:16.240
Of course.

29:16.240 --> 29:20.240
The LDF took up arms to combat censorship.

29:20.240 --> 29:22.660
But despite the MBC threat,

29:22.660 --> 29:28.250
adoption of potentially lethal job doesn't suit agents of justice.

29:28.750 --> 29:31.210
You're as smart as I thought.

29:32.840 --> 29:34.630
Your eggplant, ma'am.

29:34.630 --> 29:36.760
On that understanding,

29:37.260 --> 29:41.930
will you give me your full cooperation to protect Touma?

29:42.140 --> 29:48.270
You can start by organizing anti-censorship voices in the government.

29:48.980 --> 29:54.150
If you accept my proposal, I'll overlook your abduction plot.

29:55.570 --> 30:00.320
After all my criticism of the LDF, you want me to turn?

30:00.320 --> 30:01.950
You know what's up.

30:01.950 --> 30:09.660
Now the war has gone to court, the MBC and
the LDF are on an unavoidable collision course.

30:15.460 --> 30:17.840
What would you do?

30:17.840 --> 30:22.300
I'd seize the chance! It's an opportunity to make history!

30:24.680 --> 30:28.310
You did well to get Hikaru to give you his phone.

30:28.810 --> 30:30.690
How did you dupe him?

30:30.690 --> 30:32.150
Well...

30:32.940 --> 30:34.560
Your kisu fish, ma'am.

30:35.480 --> 30:38.650
I just did my best to hook him.

30:45.740 --> 30:47.200
Excuse me.

30:47.200 --> 30:50.910
The commander, Mr. Inamine has made coffee.

30:50.910 --> 30:52.210
Oh, thank you.

30:56.750 --> 30:59.840
I'm embarrassed to say this to you,

31:00.260 --> 31:02.050
but I'm a longtime fan.

31:02.380 --> 31:05.010
Is that so? Thank you.

31:05.010 --> 31:07.760
So, huh... if you don't mind...

31:08.180 --> 31:08.260
Nuclear Peril

31:08.510 --> 31:10.680
would you sign this?

31:12.350 --> 31:13.900
No problem.

31:17.980 --> 31:22.950
To Dojo Atsushi

31:17.980 --> 31:22.950
Touma

31:23.820 --> 31:27.870
I've always written to entertain people.

31:27.870 --> 31:30.660
I never thought I'd be censored.

31:31.500 --> 31:33.500
I can sympathize.

31:33.500 --> 31:37.130
But you have to be ready for what's coming.

31:37.790 --> 31:40.340
Being ready, for what?

31:40.710 --> 31:44.430
This time it's something completely different.

31:44.970 --> 31:48.850
The Media Betterment Act itself is on trial now,

31:48.850 --> 31:51.390
so there's no going back now.

31:52.230 --> 31:58.020
Don't give me that. I just want to go back to my regular life.

31:58.020 --> 32:00.190
It's not just about you.

32:00.360 --> 32:04.570
I don't care. I don't like this, not at all.

32:07.570 --> 32:13.540
Touma Kurato Fan Club Emergency Meeting
Resist Oppression of Free Speech!

32:14.620 --> 32:16.580
Please sign our petition!

32:20.920 --> 32:22.920
They're selling stuff too.

32:29.890 --> 32:31.760
You're that MBC agent!

32:37.230 --> 32:42.230
Let's not get too friendly here, but we ought to talk.

32:42.780 --> 32:44.780
We keep meeting like this.

32:46.950 --> 32:50.990
I'd never guess that Mr. Touma has fans in the MBC.

32:50.990 --> 32:52.450
I'm not a fan!

32:52.450 --> 32:58.120
An acquaintance asked me to keep an eye on the enemy, or something like that!

33:02.380 --> 33:06.930
So what? MBC agents have a right to read too!

33:07.260 --> 33:09.470
I didn't say anything.

33:09.970 --> 33:15.770
Plus, if I was ordered to, I'd arrest Mr. Touma.

33:15.770 --> 33:17.140
It's my job.

33:17.390 --> 33:19.400
That's what the MBC does?

33:19.980 --> 33:24.610
In this country, when the wind blows, everybody turns.

33:24.610 --> 33:26.110
Without thinking.

33:26.780 --> 33:29.740
The people who know the power of books best

33:29.740 --> 33:32.830
might be those who fear and ban them.

33:33.870 --> 33:38.960
But that doesn't justify taking away freedom of expression.

33:39.920 --> 33:41.830
I have faith.

33:41.830 --> 33:46.420
That our decisions will lead us in the right direction.

33:47.380 --> 33:51.180
Idealism like yours is harder to justify.

33:57.680 --> 33:59.980
That... What are you doing?

33:59.980 --> 34:02.020
What? Nothing, uh...

34:03.270 --> 34:03.770
This.

34:06.820 --> 34:10.280
It's so cute! How do you make it?

34:11.070 --> 34:13.070
I wonder if I can?

34:13.070 --> 34:14.990
Kasahara! Finish up first!

34:15.450 --> 34:16.830
Want to try?

34:16.830 --> 34:19.210
Please show me! How do I do it?

34:19.540 --> 34:22.170
First, do this, like this.

34:22.170 --> 34:23.330
Like this?

34:23.330 --> 34:24.630
Kasahara!

34:25.750 --> 34:26.880
It's so tricky!

34:26.880 --> 34:27.550
It's not.

34:27.550 --> 34:28.550
Really?!

34:50.700 --> 34:55.070
This garden was my late wife's pastime.

34:55.910 --> 34:59.200
I try to keep it as it was.

34:57.080 --> 35:02.540
The Hino's Nightmare: A Complete Record

35:26.980 --> 35:29.440
How's guarding Mr. Touma going?

35:29.440 --> 35:31.280
It's pretty uneventful.

35:31.280 --> 35:37.080
The trial's begun, so maybe the MBC has given up on arresting him.

35:37.080 --> 35:38.160
I don't know.

35:39.540 --> 35:42.620
That terrorism bill passed too easily.

35:43.120 --> 35:47.880
It was quite extreme, but there was no opposition at all.

35:47.880 --> 35:52.550
I wonder if this was all planned to force the law through.

35:54.130 --> 35:58.100
Like when the Media Betterment Act was passed?

35:58.100 --> 36:06.770
At any rate, those who want to expand its reach are
undoubtedly trying to use this situation to the fullest.

36:08.270 --> 36:09.190
If that's so...

36:09.570 --> 36:14.150
I doubt the MBC will simply await the verdict quietly.

36:23.370 --> 36:26.000
Picking weeds? Can I help?

36:26.000 --> 36:30.210
Oh no, that's alright! This is my part of my job.

36:30.210 --> 36:32.050
It's okay. I'm free now.

36:42.770 --> 36:48.690
By the way, I hear you're the only
female member of the LDF Task Force.

36:48.690 --> 36:51.020
Yes, right.

36:51.860 --> 36:55.610
I bet your job is dangerous, right?

36:55.610 --> 37:00.240
If you don't mind, would you tell me why you joined up?

37:01.200 --> 37:03.120
Well, it's...

37:03.120 --> 37:05.580
It's a long story.

37:05.580 --> 37:09.040
Plus, it's a little embarrassing.

37:09.290 --> 37:10.380
Please.

37:16.050 --> 37:17.260
There it is!

37:17.260 --> 37:21.720
The conclusion to my favorite fairy tale series!

37:22.970 --> 37:26.850
Executing censorship! No book leaves this store!

37:30.270 --> 37:32.230
What are you hiding?!

37:33.150 --> 37:34.440
It's a banned book!

37:35.360 --> 37:37.400
No! Give it back!

37:38.530 --> 37:42.080
Hand it over! Or you'll be arrested for theft!

37:44.200 --> 37:45.040
That's fine.

37:45.370 --> 37:46.540
What?!

37:46.540 --> 37:50.500
I'm a thief, so take me and the book to the cops!

37:51.670 --> 37:54.090
Shut up! Hand it over! Hand it over!

37:55.000 --> 37:56.260
No!

38:00.800 --> 38:02.890
This is the Kanto LDF!

38:09.100 --> 38:11.810
In my authority as a Class 3 Librarian

38:12.110 --> 38:16.280
permitted to gather literature under the Library Law,

38:16.900 --> 38:19.780
I declare these books approved!

38:27.450 --> 38:29.370
A righteous hero!

38:34.170 --> 38:35.960
Please buy this.

38:35.960 --> 38:36.920
May I?

38:38.510 --> 38:42.640
You almost become a thief to protect this book.

38:51.520 --> 38:53.860
He was so dashing,

38:54.650 --> 38:58.650
and charming and gallant and trustworthy!

38:59.610 --> 39:00.320
Is anything wrong?

39:00.820 --> 39:01.570
Uh...

39:02.530 --> 39:03.490
Is anything wrong?

39:03.490 --> 39:04.160
Huh...

39:04.780 --> 39:05.740
Um...

39:06.200 --> 39:07.990
Just like a prince,

39:09.620 --> 39:12.460
I wanted to protect books too!

39:12.830 --> 39:14.290
Just like him!

39:17.550 --> 39:20.470
I see. Thank you for telling me.

39:20.920 --> 39:24.220
Not at all! I'm sorry it was so boring.

39:24.220 --> 39:26.680
To be honest, I'm amazed.

39:27.560 --> 39:31.390
I didn't know about censorship of fairy tales.

39:31.390 --> 39:35.690
Neither about people like you striving to protect them.

39:35.690 --> 39:42.150
Really, I'm nothing compared to Instructor Dojo and my other superiors.

39:42.150 --> 39:48.200
Might your prince be Class 2 Librarian Dojo?

39:49.870 --> 39:51.540
How did you know?!

39:52.370 --> 39:54.370
So I was right!

40:00.800 --> 40:03.510
The Hino's Nightmare

40:01.800 --> 40:03.510
Does it interest you?

40:04.090 --> 40:08.430
I'm ashamed to say I don't know much about it.

40:08.430 --> 40:10.060
Don't be ashamed.

40:12.980 --> 40:13.100
The Hino's Nightmare

40:17.860 --> 40:19.770
There was no LDF then,

40:20.070 --> 40:25.570
and the MBC was not yet as openly aggressive as it is today.

40:26.450 --> 40:27.370
However,

40:36.250 --> 40:41.460
the Hino Library, active in the anti-censorship movement,

40:41.460 --> 40:45.760
was attacked by armed Media Betterment Act supporters.

40:46.340 --> 40:48.930
The library was almost defenseless.

40:51.060 --> 40:56.730
The police were called, but they only arrived when the siege was over,

40:56.730 --> 40:59.270
after the attackers had escaped.

41:00.020 --> 41:02.230
And so your wife...

41:24.710 --> 41:30.760
I may be a writer, but I'd never thought seriously about censorship.

41:31.350 --> 41:35.850
I didn't need to fight it to write entertaining novels.

41:36.020 --> 41:43.320
I thought I was being professional by not causing trouble for my publisher and others.

41:44.030 --> 41:47.650
I never realized how protected I was.

41:49.160 --> 41:49.950
By all of you.

41:50.660 --> 41:54.660
I regret what I've put Kasahara and Dojo through.

41:55.200 --> 41:58.500
I've caused so much trouble over this.

41:58.870 --> 42:01.000
You're wrong, Mr. Touma.

42:01.000 --> 42:01.830
Huh?

42:01.830 --> 42:03.380
It's a rare chance.

42:03.630 --> 42:08.340
A rare chance? The chance of a lifetime?

42:09.590 --> 42:14.680
We in the LDF take pride in having protected free expression.

42:14.890 --> 42:19.480
But the Media Betterment Act has been beyond our grasp.

42:19.730 --> 42:23.270
We couldn't fix the root of the problem.

42:23.440 --> 42:27.610
We've dragged in the young and put them in danger.

42:28.400 --> 42:30.740
I kept asking my wife.

42:31.160 --> 42:34.700
Has everything I've done been a mistake?

42:35.490 --> 42:41.210
As a writer who ignored the Media Betterment Act, I'm just as guilty.

42:41.210 --> 42:44.460
If you think so, let's fight together.

42:44.710 --> 42:50.840
For the first time, we may be able to take on the Act itself.

42:52.550 --> 42:56.220
Let's do it. For the sake of the young as well.

43:00.560 --> 43:06.190
The Hino's Nightmare

43:06.770 --> 43:08.400
I'm back!

43:08.860 --> 43:10.900
Huh? You're here today?

43:11.360 --> 43:13.870
Tonight is Komaki and Tezuka.

43:14.070 --> 43:17.080
It's tough changing shifts so often.

43:17.450 --> 43:20.040
Hey, did you get a new phone?

43:20.330 --> 43:21.580
Sort of.

43:23.210 --> 43:27.050
So, how's your prep for the appeal trial going?

43:27.340 --> 43:30.920
You know we're working with the Future Plan?

43:29.880 --> 43:30.510
Agree

43:30.220 --> 43:31.010
Neither of Them

43:30.220 --> 43:31.010
Disagree

43:30.510 --> 43:31.010
Agree

43:30.590 --> 43:31.010
Opinions About "Censorship"

43:30.920 --> 43:34.930
It's amazing. Who convinced Tezuka's brother?

43:31.010 --> 43:31.840
Opinions About "Censorship"

43:31.010 --> 43:31.840
Neither of Them

43:31.010 --> 43:31.840
Agree

43:31.010 --> 43:31.840
Disagree

43:34.930 --> 43:37.430
Tezuka didn't want to tell me.

43:37.850 --> 43:42.230
An anti-censorship faction is forming in the Diet.

43:42.690 --> 43:48.320
Only a tactician like Tezuka Satoshi could pull this off in 10 days.

43:48.320 --> 43:50.650
So we'll win the trial?

43:50.650 --> 43:52.700
It's still 50-50.

43:53.110 --> 43:55.780
But if we can win it somehow...

43:56.280 --> 43:58.450
it'll change history.

43:58.790 --> 44:00.660
You get it for once!

44:01.250 --> 44:02.870
It's a revolution!

44:03.250 --> 44:05.830
The "Library Revolution"!

44:08.250 --> 44:10.510
Gondo Tempura in Ginza!

44:10.510 --> 44:12.590
White Rose in Ebisu!

44:13.130 --> 44:14.680
Suzuki Sushi?

44:14.840 --> 44:17.640
They're all pricey! Who'd you go with?!

44:19.180 --> 44:22.270
A kind older man with a lot of money.

44:22.770 --> 44:25.270
I'll introduce him to you.

44:25.270 --> 44:30.150
Shibasaki! What are you up to behind my back?

44:33.070 --> 44:37.530
20 Days Until The Appeal Trial Verdict

44:37.530 --> 44:38.780
Animal Encyclopedia

44:41.790 --> 44:43.200
I'll read this one next.

44:43.200 --> 44:44.080
Right.

44:44.620 --> 44:49.040
Like caviar to a monkey. She just likes the characters.

44:49.170 --> 44:51.500
Really?! Not a monkey, it's a Cat!

44:51.500 --> 44:53.840
You look like a monkey to me!

44:55.380 --> 44:56.510
The characters?

44:57.090 --> 45:03.520
Glimpses of romantic rivalries and male friendships in between the main story!

45:03.520 --> 45:05.890
I like following characters.

45:06.020 --> 45:09.360
That's why you forget the main story!

45:09.520 --> 45:12.570
Well, I skip the difficult parts.

45:12.860 --> 45:15.200
See! She's such a person!

45:15.900 --> 45:19.490
Read it any way you like, as long as you enjoy it.

45:20.660 --> 45:24.330
So which characters are your favorite?

45:24.330 --> 45:26.710
You really want to know?!

45:26.710 --> 45:32.750
The hero's friend in "Nuclear Peril".
He's manly, but likes ice cream bars!

45:33.090 --> 45:37.430
That line at the end, "If I live, I'll eat a box of them!"

45:37.430 --> 45:40.220
Moreover, It's so dreamy!

45:40.390 --> 45:42.220
Dreamily contradictory!

45:42.260 --> 45:45.890
Wait a minute, what is "dreamily contradictory"?

45:46.430 --> 45:49.150
No
Feeding

45:46.430 --> 45:49.150
Fishing Is
Prohibited

45:50.360 --> 45:56.570
7 Days Until The Appeal Trial Verdict

45:56.780 --> 45:59.610
Sir, you'll have mayonnaise, right?

45:59.610 --> 46:00.990
Thank you.

46:00.990 --> 46:05.540
Are you a mayoholic? Do you put it on fried eggs?

46:05.750 --> 46:09.250
I ask for sugar on my fried eggs.

46:10.790 --> 46:14.590
That's crazy! Ketchup goes with fried eggs.

46:15.050 --> 46:17.920
You're not exactly normal yourself.

46:17.920 --> 46:20.720
My parents also ate them that way.

46:21.090 --> 46:24.600
There wasn't much nutritious food back then.

46:26.600 --> 46:29.350
Would you like some more, sir?

46:29.350 --> 46:31.060
Oh, yes please.

46:31.100 --> 46:34.070
Instructor! I'll get it for him.

46:34.070 --> 46:37.360
Don't move! Sit your clumsy self down!

46:38.150 --> 46:40.780
Mr. Touma's clumsier than I am.

46:41.110 --> 46:42.160
H-hey!

46:43.910 --> 46:46.370
It's alright, it's the truth!

46:46.490 --> 46:49.290
Hey, I'll slice some pickles.

46:49.580 --> 46:55.250
Turnip for Mr. Touma, and eggplant for Commander Inamine, right?

47:03.470 --> 47:07.720
Today some men, probably MBC agents, forced me

47:07.720 --> 47:10.520
to tell them about Mr. Touma.

47:10.520 --> 47:12.020
I'm so sorry.

47:12.020 --> 47:15.770
The clock in the living room is bugged.

47:16.020 --> 47:17.980
Please forgive me.

47:48.140 --> 47:49.310
Welcome.

47:51.180 --> 47:52.310
Inamine?!

47:52.310 --> 47:55.770
Sorry I'm not the man you're looking for.

47:55.770 --> 47:59.820
Now you're here, you'll be my entertainment.

48:01.440 --> 48:03.070
This is Hino.

48:03.070 --> 48:07.370
Where the Media Betterment Act took away all I had.

48:08.660 --> 48:10.410
Stop. Don't shoot!

48:10.580 --> 48:12.370
Please don't move.

48:12.620 --> 48:17.290
You're intruders in this house where my wife's memory rests.

48:17.750 --> 48:22.090
I'm barely holding back from pulling the trigger.

48:22.420 --> 48:26.970
But if you try anything, I can't guarantee I won't.

48:34.730 --> 48:36.350
And another one!

48:37.940 --> 48:38.900
Kasahara!

48:38.900 --> 48:39.730
Yes sir!

48:45.110 --> 48:48.030
Be more careful! You'll hurt your arm!

48:48.070 --> 48:48.830
I'm fine!

48:49.240 --> 48:50.450
Do we return to base?

48:51.080 --> 48:54.250
Too dangerous. We'll go to Tachikawa.

48:54.250 --> 48:57.250
Tachikawa? But it's back that way!

49:09.760 --> 49:10.850
Go away!

49:11.350 --> 49:13.220
Here goes! Grit your teeth!

49:35.290 --> 49:38.790
It'll be shaky, we'll be there in 10 minutes!

49:39.830 --> 49:44.630
Shaking's fine, but I'm a little claustrophobic.

49:45.800 --> 49:49.930
Me too! But it'll be quick, so let's hang in there!

50:05.490 --> 50:06.400
Instructor!

50:06.400 --> 50:09.070
I know. The helo's under attack.

50:12.530 --> 50:14.790
What if it crashes on us?!

50:14.990 --> 50:21.330
Don't worry! No matter how dangerous it gets, our pilots will protect us!

50:23.130 --> 50:26.170
Mr. Touma, we'll protect you at any cost.

50:27.220 --> 50:30.260
So, please write a new novel!

50:45.230 --> 50:49.360
If anyone sees me now, I'll bite my tongue and die!

50:51.740 --> 50:53.030
Detach!

51:21.230 --> 51:23.060
Hey, well done!

51:24.690 --> 51:26.230
Captain Genda?!

51:27.940 --> 51:29.320
Now I get it.

51:29.320 --> 51:34.120
I had serious déjà vu when I heard how crazy the plan was.

51:34.120 --> 51:38.160
You're still injured, so what are you doing here?

51:38.580 --> 51:42.830
I can't just lie in bed with all this going on.

51:42.830 --> 51:43.960
But...

51:43.960 --> 51:47.380
I told him as soon as I got your message.

51:47.710 --> 51:50.050
I never thought he'd come.

51:50.050 --> 51:52.630
Of course he was going to come!

51:52.630 --> 51:55.350
Did you even get permission?!

51:55.890 --> 51:58.260
I apologized to the hospital!

51:58.260 --> 52:01.270
Don't be mad, we just got reunited.

52:01.270 --> 52:02.600
But...

52:02.890 --> 52:04.940
What about Commander Inamine?

52:05.270 --> 52:07.190
Relax, he's safe.

52:07.190 --> 52:09.320
One pilot got shot.

52:09.530 --> 52:12.110
The bullet needs to be removed.

52:12.570 --> 52:14.320
The other broke his arm.

52:14.320 --> 52:17.450
Both are in hospital, but nothing life threatening.

52:18.240 --> 52:19.450
I'm so glad!

52:20.450 --> 52:23.620
Ogata, let me take command from here.

52:24.080 --> 52:26.000
I feel like I already did.

52:37.100 --> 52:40.970
If the helicopter had fallen...

52:41.470 --> 52:44.690
Was the MBC trying to kill us?

52:45.140 --> 52:48.150
They were only shooting at the helo.

52:49.150 --> 52:52.490
In battle, there's no room to think about

52:52.690 --> 52:55.860
who's on board, or that they could die.

52:57.160 --> 52:58.990
I'd probably be the same.

52:59.530 --> 53:02.330
No! You're different!

53:02.660 --> 53:04.120
It's not just me.

53:04.160 --> 53:08.500
When you shoot someone, do you worry about hurting them?

53:19.550 --> 53:22.020
It's not just about you.

53:24.270 --> 53:27.440
Mr. Touma, we'll protect you at any cost.

53:27.690 --> 53:30.860
Promise me you'll write a new novel!

53:39.240 --> 53:39.700
First, watch this footage.

53:39.700 --> 53:42.160
Media Betterment Act thoroughly examined!

53:39.700 --> 53:42.160
Exclusive footage obtained

53:39.700 --> 53:42.160
First, watch this footage.

53:42.160 --> 53:53.840
Picture source       .      Kanto Library Force

53:43.290 --> 53:46.370
<i>Pilot hit! Clear the landing area!</i>

53:49.000 --> 53:50.630
<i>Touchdown! Cut engines!</i>

53:50.630 --> 53:53.840
<i>All stand clear until rotors stop!</i>

53:54.260 --> 53:58.380
This was provided to us this morning by the LDF,

53:58.380 --> 54:04.220
whose helicopter came under attack from MBC troops last night

54:04.220 --> 54:07.890
while transporting Touma Kurato to their base.

54:08.560 --> 54:16.280
Media Betterment Act thoroughly examined!

54:08.560 --> 54:16.280
Exclusive footage obtained

54:08.980 --> 54:12.400
There have been previous claims of

54:12.400 --> 54:16.280
MBC attempts to forcibly prevent Touma from writing,

54:16.650 --> 54:19.860
but this footage is undeniable proof.

54:19.860 --> 54:24.830
Not only is Touma's right to write in danger, but also his life.

54:25.580 --> 54:31.000
Plus, isn't freedom of expression guaranteed by the Constitution?

54:31.540 --> 54:38.260
It is bizarre that such concerns haven't been represented in the media until now.

54:38.880 --> 54:46.930
Wow! I've never seen explicit accusations at the level of Media Betterment Committee on TV before.

54:46.930 --> 54:49.440
Even with the footage, why now?

54:49.440 --> 54:51.400
It's all thanks to her.

54:52.110 --> 54:57.570
I persuaded the station to fight against the Media Betterment Act.

54:57.570 --> 55:00.530
Really?! Won't they be targeted?

55:00.530 --> 55:02.870
That's the trickiest part.

55:02.870 --> 55:06.740
If they're taken off air, they'll lose income.

55:06.870 --> 55:11.790
But if people take interest, they'll gain more than they lose.

55:12.330 --> 55:16.340
We've just received official notice from the MBC.

55:16.880 --> 55:19.670
As our reporting was inappropriate,

55:19.670 --> 55:23.680
we have been banned from broadcasting tomorrow.

55:23.680 --> 55:25.810
They didn't waste time!

55:26.060 --> 55:28.140
But it doesn't stop there.

55:28.430 --> 55:33.940
All commercial stations are criticizing the Media Betterment Act.

55:34.440 --> 55:35.770
They've got loads of ammo.

55:36.520 --> 55:39.780
If they show all their unseen footage,

55:40.200 --> 55:41.950
it'll last till the trial's over.

55:43.870 --> 55:46.830
Either the media bends, or the law.

55:47.240 --> 55:48.620
No turning back now.

55:51.250 --> 55:54.670
Media Betterment Act v.s. Free Expression?

55:58.170 --> 56:01.510
No broadcasts today due to MBC sanctions.

56:04.260 --> 56:06.930
For a censorship-free society . . .

56:07.510 --> 56:11.520
It's annoying not being able to watch what I want.

56:11.940 --> 56:15.150
I guess it's unavoidable though.

56:15.360 --> 56:20.110
I was surprised! It's all a bit over my head.

56:20.280 --> 56:26.320
I'm not a fan of Touma Kurato, so I thought it had nothing to do with me.

56:26.320 --> 56:33.290
Reconsider
Censorship<i>!</i>

56:26.620 --> 56:28.910
Now, our guest commentator,

56:28.910 --> 56:33.040
Justice Ministry Media Betterment Act issues adviser

56:33.290 --> 56:37.880
and Library Future Plan chairman, Mr. Tezuka Satoshi.

56:33.460 --> 56:40.000
Tezuka Satoshi (Future Library Committee Representative)

56:38.590 --> 56:40.000
Good to be here.

56:42.470 --> 56:45.180
Once in an interviewee I mentioned that...

56:45.720 --> 56:51.140
censorship and the Media Betterment Act don't affect each other.

56:51.470 --> 56:54.810
The Act is steeped in such apathy,

56:54.810 --> 56:58.570
tricking the public into ignoring its dangers,

56:58.570 --> 57:01.070
and violations of free speech.

57:01.280 --> 57:04.900
The fearless and openly defiant stance

57:04.900 --> 57:09.780
taken by the influential medium of television against the Act

57:09.780 --> 57:12.250
is a bold and historic step.

57:12.790 --> 57:14.000
Thank you.

57:14.330 --> 57:17.580
Your brother is pretty telegenic.

57:17.580 --> 57:19.790
He's a formidable enemy,

57:19.790 --> 57:23.420
but as an ally, there's nobody more reliable.

57:23.420 --> 57:27.890
I'm worried his smug posing will put the public off.

57:27.890 --> 57:31.430
Why don't you admit he has good qualities too?

57:33.810 --> 57:38.440
Please sign our petition against persecution of Mr. Touma!

57:38.860 --> 57:40.770
Please sign here!

57:44.530 --> 57:46.150
Firm objection to
Betterment Act

57:47.610 --> 57:49.370
Please help!

57:51.490 --> 57:53.950
Please sign our petition!

58:00.630 --> 58:03.590
The day Of The Appeal Trial Verdict

58:02.300 --> 58:09.430
A verdict was reached today in the Touma free speech appeal trial.

58:03.590 --> 58:09.430
Appeal Trial Verdict "Freedom of Expression" Rejected

58:11.550 --> 58:15.600
I know it's hard to sue the government and win,

58:16.270 --> 58:18.230
but to lose so easily!

58:18.690 --> 58:20.940
It's already on to the next stage.

58:21.900 --> 58:23.400
The next is the Supreme Court.

58:24.230 --> 58:26.320
What did my brother say?

58:26.780 --> 58:30.700
The High Court judge was in favor of the Act.

58:30.910 --> 58:35.660
But I doubt they'll be able to rig the trial this time.

58:36.250 --> 58:39.330
Now all we can do is hope.

58:43.420 --> 58:50.130
The MBC says that this measure is only temporary until the terrorists are found.

58:50.130 --> 58:53.140
But, it is effectively indefinite.

58:53.560 --> 59:00.400
If so, then our Constitution has been subverted by the fear of terrorism.

59:00.400 --> 59:02.360
You're quite right.

59:02.360 --> 59:05.230
The world will laugh at Japan.

59:05.230 --> 59:09.950
Emergency discussion!
Tezuka Satoshi
Live Appearance

59:05.610 --> 59:08.280
Just as the terrorists wanted.

59:08.280 --> 59:14.990
However, that assumes these terrorists actually exist.

59:14.990 --> 59:16.740
What do you mean?

59:27.550 --> 59:28.800
Tezuka!

59:29.090 --> 59:30.510
You're gonna die!

59:36.810 --> 59:38.980
Now in breaking news,

59:38.980 --> 59:44.310
Library Future Plan chairman Tezuka Satoshi

59:44.310 --> 59:46.940
Tezuka Satoshi (Future Library Committee) stabbed!

59:44.310 --> 59:46.940
URGENT

59:44.310 --> 59:46.940
REPORT

59:44.310 --> 59:46.940
DLT News

59:44.310 --> 59:46.940
has just been stabbed near our studio's entrance.

59:51.360 --> 59:59.830
Tezuka Satoshi (Future Library Committee) stabbed!

59:51.650 --> 59:54.870
One moment please. I've been told...

59:55.660 --> 59:57.910
Mr. Tezuka, are you alright?

59:57.910 --> 01:00:01.000
There's not a scratch on me.

01:00:01.000 --> 01:00:07.500
But my LDF bodyguard was injured and has been rushed to hospital.

01:00:07.500 --> 01:00:10.090
It's not life-threatening.

01:00:15.510 --> 01:00:15.600
Incoming Call

01:00:15.510 --> 01:00:15.600
Tezuka Hikaru

01:00:18.720 --> 01:00:20.230
Ms. Shibasaki?

01:00:20.230 --> 01:00:21.060
It's me.

01:00:21.060 --> 01:00:21.940
Hikaru?

01:00:23.100 --> 01:00:26.310
I don't want you to die, so stay safe!

01:00:26.310 --> 01:00:28.730
Don't let everybody down.

01:00:30.740 --> 01:00:35.070
You take care too. Say hi to Ms. Shibasaki for me.

01:00:35.700 --> 01:00:36.570
Like hell!

01:00:38.540 --> 01:00:41.080
What a cute little exchange.

01:00:41.080 --> 01:00:42.000
Shut up!

01:00:42.290 --> 01:00:47.460
Hey, you asked me to be here. What a cheek!

01:00:48.550 --> 01:00:52.420
Shibasaki, sometimes you talk like an old woman.

01:00:52.920 --> 01:00:54.260
How rude!

01:00:54.260 --> 01:00:58.140
How could you say that to me?! Like an o-old...

01:01:00.850 --> 01:01:01.600
Thanks.

01:01:02.310 --> 01:01:03.310
Good night.

01:01:07.440 --> 01:01:12.570
9 Days Until The Supreme Court Verdict

01:01:14.280 --> 01:01:15.780
You got nothing?!

01:01:16.200 --> 01:01:19.490
No ideas about what to do if we lose?

01:01:19.490 --> 01:01:21.330
Sir! A question!

01:01:21.330 --> 01:01:22.370
Bring it!

01:01:22.950 --> 01:01:26.580
Shouldn't the top brass come up with an idea?

01:01:26.960 --> 01:01:30.170
They think inside the box!

01:01:30.170 --> 01:01:34.550
So we'll back them up with our flexible thinking.

01:01:34.550 --> 01:01:38.800
Don't believe a word of it. He just can't sit still.

01:01:38.800 --> 01:01:40.010
I know that!

01:01:42.970 --> 01:01:45.690
Why not just withdraw the case?

01:01:46.190 --> 01:01:49.900
Mr. Touma could list our base as his address.

01:01:50.690 --> 01:01:53.360
We could make him an LDF member.

01:01:53.360 --> 01:01:54.740
No, no!

01:01:54.740 --> 01:01:57.860
Can't you think of anything fresher?

01:01:58.870 --> 01:02:04.120
If even a Supreme Court verdict can't protect free speech,

01:02:04.120 --> 01:02:08.040
why not have Mr. Touma seek asylum overseas?

01:02:11.540 --> 01:02:13.050
Say that again.

01:02:13.050 --> 01:02:16.340
Huh? Did I say something bad?

01:02:16.510 --> 01:02:18.260
Come on, say it again!

01:02:18.260 --> 01:02:21.850
I don't know what for, but I apologize!

01:02:21.850 --> 01:02:24.140
I won't get angry! Say it!

01:02:24.140 --> 01:02:26.520
You're already angry!

01:02:26.520 --> 01:02:29.060
Dojo, it's not an interrogation.

01:02:29.100 --> 01:02:31.270
You said asylum, didn't you?

01:02:31.440 --> 01:02:34.480
I might have, or I might not have.

01:02:34.730 --> 01:02:36.950
That's today's best idea!

01:02:38.700 --> 01:02:41.870
Impressive for a mind like yours!

01:02:44.580 --> 01:02:50.420
If you're impressed, why should you grill me like that?!

01:02:56.010 --> 01:02:59.470
I'll have to ask my wife and son.

01:03:00.130 --> 01:03:02.890
Of course. This is very sudden.

01:03:03.050 --> 01:03:07.890
But if no one can read my work as long as I'm in this country,

01:03:08.520 --> 01:03:10.690
I have no other choice.

01:03:11.810 --> 01:03:12.940
Mr. Touma!

01:03:14.820 --> 01:03:17.360
The top brass love the plan.

01:03:17.360 --> 01:03:21.610
But they were stunned when I said it was Kasahara's.

01:03:21.610 --> 01:03:24.450
Asylum never crossed my mind.

01:03:25.540 --> 01:03:27.910
What's the response overseas?

01:03:29.290 --> 01:03:32.750
The International Library League are on it.

01:03:32.750 --> 01:03:35.670
The Netherlands, Sweden, Britain,

01:03:36.340 --> 01:03:39.630
and the United States should be receptive.

01:03:40.090 --> 01:03:43.260
Good! First, a Supreme Court victory.

01:03:43.640 --> 01:03:49.270
But if we lose, we get Mr. Touma safely out of Japan right away.

01:03:49.730 --> 01:03:50.730
Understood?

01:03:50.730 --> 01:03:51.600
Yes sir!

01:03:59.690 --> 01:04:03.160
The Day Of The Supreme Court Verdict

01:04:03.160 --> 01:04:05.620
Heavy Wind Alert

01:04:08.750 --> 01:04:14.000
The Supreme Court Media Betterment Act trial verdict is imminent.

01:04:21.510 --> 01:04:23.470
The verdict is out!

01:04:24.260 --> 01:04:29.020
As a temporary measure until the terrorists are identified,

01:04:29.020 --> 01:04:34.150
Mr. Touma will be prohibited from writing for the next 5 years.

01:04:34.440 --> 01:04:38.860
Touma Kurato loses appeal!

01:04:34.440 --> 01:04:38.860
Quick
Report

01:04:34.650 --> 01:04:38.860
This is effectively a defeat for the plaintiff.

01:04:39.190 --> 01:04:40.280
Alright, let's go!

01:04:46.570 --> 01:04:47.990
Mr. Touma!

01:04:49.040 --> 01:04:51.000
A few words on the verdict!

01:04:51.450 --> 01:04:53.670
Save it for the press conference.

01:05:12.850 --> 01:05:14.810
It's raining so hard.

01:05:15.440 --> 01:05:17.730
A record downpour, I hear.

01:05:18.360 --> 01:05:20.400
Perfect for a covert mission.

01:05:20.400 --> 01:05:23.900
Don't stick your face next to your superior's!

01:05:24.400 --> 01:05:25.740
You ain't a kid!

01:05:25.990 --> 01:05:28.030
First, the Dutch Embassy.

01:05:32.750 --> 01:05:34.830
Barricades! It's the MBC!

01:05:36.500 --> 01:05:37.710
Halt!

01:05:43.130 --> 01:05:45.880
It's no good! Head for the next one!

01:05:50.890 --> 01:05:51.680
It's them!

01:05:52.350 --> 01:05:53.140
Dammit!

01:06:04.440 --> 01:06:06.150
Ditch the car and run!

01:06:06.450 --> 01:06:08.200
Dojo, Kasahara, take him!

01:06:08.740 --> 01:06:11.660
I'll slow them down! Tezuka can do it!

01:06:11.870 --> 01:06:13.240
Shut up and go!

01:06:15.710 --> 01:06:17.420
Mr. Touma, this way!

01:06:23.460 --> 01:06:25.470
Head underground to base!

01:06:32.600 --> 01:06:36.480
The British Embassy's near Hanzomon Station.

01:06:37.690 --> 01:06:42.150
I know it's dangerous. It's not a sane choice.

01:06:42.770 --> 01:06:45.820
But if I don't act now, I'm done for!

01:06:46.360 --> 01:06:50.280
Vice Captain Ogata told us to protect Mr. Touma,

01:06:50.320 --> 01:06:52.280
not to return him to base!

01:06:55.830 --> 01:06:57.120
Let's go!

01:07:17.810 --> 01:07:20.060
Oh, come on. It sucks!

01:07:23.570 --> 01:07:25.190
It's a no-go here too.

01:07:26.110 --> 01:07:27.820
Hey! You there!

01:07:28.990 --> 01:07:31.450
Your umbrella broke? Use this.

01:07:34.410 --> 01:07:35.620
Y-You're...

01:07:42.380 --> 01:07:43.500
I'm sorry.

01:07:43.710 --> 01:07:47.510
You worried about my umbrella... Forgive me.

01:07:47.960 --> 01:07:51.340
Even so, we're still enemies.

01:07:51.890 --> 01:07:53.550
Mr. Touma, hurry!

01:08:05.610 --> 01:08:06.690
Dojo!

01:08:08.860 --> 01:08:11.910
I'll hold them off! Go!

01:08:11.910 --> 01:08:13.570
You'll bleed to death!

01:08:13.870 --> 01:08:15.660
Forget about me! Go!

01:08:16.080 --> 01:08:16.910
No!

01:08:17.290 --> 01:08:19.500
So you bastards fired?!

01:08:20.040 --> 01:08:21.870
Let's go while we can!

01:08:30.470 --> 01:08:32.590
Instructor, forgive me!

01:08:36.390 --> 01:08:37.930
Doors closing.

01:08:49.150 --> 01:08:51.950
I'm sorry, he's hurt. Please move.

01:08:55.910 --> 01:08:58.620
What's going on? Is he injured?

01:09:01.500 --> 01:09:03.290
He's bleeding bad!

01:09:03.960 --> 01:09:05.750
He won't make it!

01:09:08.420 --> 01:09:10.300
They're on the platform.

01:09:10.550 --> 01:09:13.720
We'd better get off before Shinjuku.

01:09:17.050 --> 01:09:21.100
Let's get off one stop before. I have an idea.

01:09:29.610 --> 01:09:30.780
Dojo?!

01:09:32.780 --> 01:09:35.910
Sorry to ask, but can you put us up?

01:09:35.910 --> 01:09:39.120
Are you okay?! I'll call an ambulance!

01:09:39.120 --> 01:09:41.870
Wait! It's too dangerous now.

01:09:43.200 --> 01:09:44.290
This way!

01:09:48.130 --> 01:09:51.670
Mr. Touma, any ideas about what to do now?

01:09:54.800 --> 01:10:00.600
There are a few consulates in Osaka that also have diplomatic immunity.

01:10:00.600 --> 01:10:02.390
Right! That could work.

01:10:03.850 --> 01:10:06.270
But it doesn't matter.

01:10:06.270 --> 01:10:10.230
I can't leave you. If I persevere for 5 years...

01:10:10.230 --> 01:10:11.110
No!

01:10:12.150 --> 01:10:17.160
After 5 years they'll find a new excuse to extend your ban!

01:10:17.160 --> 01:10:20.370
They'll do the same to other writers!

01:10:20.370 --> 01:10:21.990
It's now or never!

01:10:24.000 --> 01:10:25.160
Dojo...

01:10:25.580 --> 01:10:26.790
Please go!

01:10:27.420 --> 01:10:28.670
But I...

01:10:31.920 --> 01:10:32.590
Kasahara?

01:10:33.590 --> 01:10:35.300
Got your license?

01:10:35.300 --> 01:10:36.550
Y-Yes.

01:10:37.680 --> 01:10:38.720
You can do it.

01:10:43.850 --> 01:10:45.230
I can't...

01:10:46.020 --> 01:10:50.650
I can't leave him this way and take Mr. Touma to Osaka alone!

01:11:06.120 --> 01:11:11.710
I think he's kind to me because
he recognizes the effort I've put in.

01:11:12.840 --> 01:11:16.050
And that's enough for me.

01:11:23.050 --> 01:11:25.100
It's alright. I can do it.

01:11:30.730 --> 01:11:31.900
Instructor!

01:11:32.810 --> 01:11:34.070
Don't look sad.

01:11:34.690 --> 01:11:38.280
My wound's not nearly as bad as the Captain's.

01:11:38.990 --> 01:11:41.410
This isn't the time for jokes!

01:11:41.740 --> 01:11:45.030
If only it'd hit your bulletproof vest!

01:11:47.250 --> 01:11:48.120
Don't cry.

01:11:48.500 --> 01:11:52.540
Smile. You're Mr. Touma's only protector from here on.

01:11:55.300 --> 01:11:56.630
Stay focused.

01:12:03.390 --> 01:12:05.310
Uh, by the way...

01:12:05.310 --> 01:12:07.020
You wanted this, right?

01:12:07.720 --> 01:12:10.480
It's a loan. Better bring it back.

01:12:18.530 --> 01:12:19.780
You can do it.

01:12:23.410 --> 01:12:24.820
I know you can.

01:12:51.310 --> 01:12:53.020
Instructor...

01:12:53.900 --> 01:12:54.980
When I...

01:12:55.480 --> 01:13:00.320
When I return, I'll give it back and tell you I love you!

01:13:00.320 --> 01:13:03.150
So please, make sure you pull through!

01:13:03.910 --> 01:13:07.160
If you don't, I'll never forgive you!

01:13:22.420 --> 01:13:26.260
Don't worry, Maki. If anyone can do it, they can.

01:13:29.680 --> 01:13:33.980
This looks easy to drive, plus it's got a GPS system.

01:13:36.020 --> 01:13:39.360
Glad I made it! Here's some tea and food.

01:13:39.360 --> 01:13:44.200
Plus other bits and pieces. A map of Osaka, a guide book.

01:13:44.200 --> 01:13:46.320
That'll help. Thank you.

01:13:46.660 --> 01:13:48.070
I appreciate it.

01:13:49.450 --> 01:13:52.080
Oh, and you forgot this.

01:13:59.840 --> 01:14:01.210
It's lovely.

01:14:01.920 --> 01:14:04.550
Instructor Dojo bought it for me.

01:14:05.930 --> 01:14:08.220
Knowing you, you'll be fine.

01:14:09.970 --> 01:14:12.930
Please take care of Instructor Dojo.

01:14:32.990 --> 01:14:37.920
The Tomei Expressway's crowded, so the Chuo will be faster.

01:14:37.920 --> 01:14:40.790
Is that different to what the GPS says?

01:14:40.790 --> 01:14:43.840
The Shinjuku Interchange is coming up.

01:14:43.840 --> 01:14:45.670
Where?! Where?!

01:14:46.130 --> 01:14:48.470
Wait, I'll get the map out.

01:14:51.390 --> 01:14:53.310
Green sign detected!

01:14:53.310 --> 01:14:54.930
Found you!

01:14:55.480 --> 01:14:57.390
This route is incorrect.

01:14:57.390 --> 01:14:59.480
Shut the hell up!

01:15:01.860 --> 01:15:06.110
You have entered the Shuto Expressway. Go straight.

01:15:07.240 --> 01:15:09.910
Who needs GPS when you've got smarts?

01:15:10.110 --> 01:15:12.780
Or rather, animal instinct!

01:15:14.290 --> 01:15:16.120
How will you call base?

01:15:16.120 --> 01:15:18.670
My mobile's water damaged.

01:15:18.670 --> 01:15:21.460
Landlines might be tapped.

01:15:29.130 --> 01:15:33.850
Then the question is, how did they try to get back to base?

01:15:34.140 --> 01:15:37.020
Most likely, they rode the subway.

01:15:37.350 --> 01:15:43.110
Wait! If they got off at Hanzomon, the British Embassy's right there.

01:15:43.110 --> 01:15:47.820
That's too dangerous! Dojo wouldn't do something like that!

01:15:48.070 --> 01:15:50.820
If I'd gone, I could've stopped him.

01:15:51.160 --> 01:15:55.740
But if Mr. Touma hadn't given up on seeking asylum,

01:15:56.040 --> 01:15:58.500
Dojo would've thought twice.

01:15:58.500 --> 01:16:01.750
And if Kasahara was there with him,

01:16:02.250 --> 01:16:04.880
she'd have told him to go for it.

01:16:05.300 --> 01:16:08.760
And her words would've spurred him on.

01:16:08.760 --> 01:16:11.340
You mean they make a bad duo?

01:16:11.340 --> 01:16:14.050
They're a great duo, beyond doubt.

01:16:14.050 --> 01:16:16.510
That's why they didn't return.

01:16:21.690 --> 01:16:23.690
We're in Yamanashi.

01:16:24.360 --> 01:16:26.900
The rain's eased off quite a lot.

01:16:27.320 --> 01:16:29.070
Yes, you're right.

01:16:34.240 --> 01:16:35.410
Ms. Kasahara?

01:16:35.410 --> 01:16:36.200
Yes!

01:16:36.200 --> 01:16:40.870
I thought censorship was just something you worked around.

01:16:41.410 --> 01:16:44.420
That a pro's job was to work around it.

01:16:44.420 --> 01:16:48.800
I had no idea that your people were protecting books.

01:16:48.800 --> 01:16:50.720
I feel so ashamed.

01:16:51.170 --> 01:16:52.840
Please, don't.

01:16:53.470 --> 01:16:56.100
You like fairy tales, don't you?

01:16:56.100 --> 01:16:57.100
Yes sir!

01:16:58.060 --> 01:17:00.850
I read them a lot as a child too.

01:17:01.560 --> 01:17:08.480
So I think I'll make my next book a kind of fantasy for young children.

01:17:08.480 --> 01:17:09.570
Sir!

01:17:10.780 --> 01:17:14.740
Once upon a time, there lived an old troubadour.

01:17:15.410 --> 01:17:18.240
Do you know what a troubadour is?

01:17:18.240 --> 01:17:22.210
Yes sir! They often appear in fantasy stories.

01:17:22.210 --> 01:17:24.710
Like a storytelling minstrel.

01:17:24.710 --> 01:17:26.330
Hmm, that's right.

01:17:26.330 --> 01:17:29.590
In a way, they're authors too.

01:17:30.760 --> 01:17:35.930
In this land there were many troubadours, and plentiful music.

01:17:36.430 --> 01:17:37.760
That's wonderful!

01:17:38.930 --> 01:17:43.560
But one day, the king forbade them from singing.

01:17:43.560 --> 01:17:48.110
By decree, only songs approved by the king could be sung.

01:17:48.940 --> 01:17:54.900
Troubadours who sang freely in defiance were jailed one after another.

01:17:54.950 --> 01:17:56.320
How cruel.

01:17:56.780 --> 01:18:02.200
The old troubadour simply watched as his friends were imprisoned.

01:18:03.040 --> 01:18:06.290
He blamed them for singing in defiance.

01:18:07.210 --> 01:18:08.210
However,

01:18:08.460 --> 01:18:12.300
despite his obedience in singing approved songs,

01:18:12.300 --> 01:18:15.010
the royal guards came one day.

01:18:16.630 --> 01:18:20.680
Someone had caused trouble using one of his songs,

01:18:20.680 --> 01:18:23.310
and so he was to be punished.

01:18:24.350 --> 01:18:28.810
For the first time, he regretted abandoning his friends.

01:18:29.360 --> 01:18:31.360
But it was too late.

01:18:33.320 --> 01:18:38.360
Then suddenly, knights bearing a bluebird insignia appeared.

01:18:43.660 --> 01:18:47.710
They had been outcast for opposing the song ban,

01:18:47.710 --> 01:18:50.500
and had come to save the troubadour.

01:18:52.340 --> 01:18:55.590
These knights were gallant and noble.

01:18:55.590 --> 01:18:56.510
Yes sir!

01:18:58.050 --> 01:18:59.930
This is the first time for me.

01:18:59.930 --> 01:19:06.230
wanting to write a story that everyone will love, and not merely for profit.

01:19:25.790 --> 01:19:29.370
Got it! They're heading for Osaka.

01:19:30.170 --> 01:19:32.920
If only we could contact them...

01:19:36.260 --> 01:19:39.880
Lake Suwa
Service Area

01:19:42.180 --> 01:19:43.560
This'll do.

01:19:48.430 --> 01:19:51.650
Won't payphones be tapped too?

01:19:51.650 --> 01:19:55.110
Yes, but I've thought of another way.

01:19:55.110 --> 01:20:00.030
It'll be a little tricky, but my colleagues will work it out.

01:20:00.030 --> 01:20:00.530
Huh!

01:20:03.490 --> 01:20:07.700
Amazing. What a lovely starry sky after the typhoon.

01:20:10.000 --> 01:20:12.040
Will doing this end it?

01:20:13.210 --> 01:20:15.250
Instructor Dojo asked me.

01:20:15.840 --> 01:20:20.760
"When you shoot someone, do you worry about hurting them?"

01:20:21.720 --> 01:20:26.720
If we talked to MBC agents, we'd realize they're people too.

01:20:28.850 --> 01:20:32.400
Even so, I can't just put down my gun.

01:20:33.440 --> 01:20:36.730
We should have done something about this.

01:20:38.480 --> 01:20:40.450
Before things got so bad.

01:20:46.450 --> 01:20:48.450
A message from Kasahara!

01:20:49.120 --> 01:20:50.500
She sent this!

01:20:50.500 --> 01:20:51.620
What's that?

01:20:52.960 --> 01:20:54.960
A telegram to you?

01:20:55.250 --> 01:20:58.380
Who the hell is this Asami Shibasaki?

01:20:59.010 --> 01:21:03.430
It's Kasahara! I don't know anyone called Asami!

01:21:07.310 --> 01:21:09.720
Damn noise! Ogata, rip it up!

01:21:09.720 --> 01:21:10.770
Yes sir.

01:21:15.980 --> 01:21:18.360
What's this?! A code?!

01:21:19.820 --> 01:21:25.070
Kasahara must've racked her brain over this. I'll look into it!

01:21:25.070 --> 01:21:26.620
Nanba

01:21:25.070 --> 01:21:26.620
Nankaidori Shopping Arcade

01:21:33.920 --> 01:21:37.210
Excuse me, I have a strange request.

01:21:37.210 --> 01:21:38.420
Yes ma'am?

01:21:38.420 --> 01:21:40.170
Whatever it costs,

01:21:40.170 --> 01:21:43.760
make him the least conspicuous man in Osaka!

01:21:45.010 --> 01:21:47.180
You're really going all out!

01:21:48.560 --> 01:21:52.480
So, you want to conceal this gentleman's identity?

01:21:52.730 --> 01:21:53.730
Yes!

01:21:53.730 --> 01:21:57.020
Then you should try that store over there.

01:22:02.740 --> 01:22:05.820
I never thought I'd end up like this.

01:22:05.820 --> 01:22:10.410
Well, this is the least conspicuous outfit in Osaka.

01:22:12.370 --> 01:22:14.120
One last check.

01:22:14.500 --> 01:22:17.540
First, head to the British Consulate.

01:22:17.540 --> 01:22:20.460
If it's no good, head north this way

01:22:20.460 --> 01:22:23.090
for the US and Dutch consulates.

01:22:23.300 --> 01:22:25.340
We go right on 12 noon.

01:22:25.680 --> 01:22:29.970
In that get-up, you're less conspicuous on your own.

01:22:29.970 --> 01:22:31.720
Walk in confidently.

01:22:31.890 --> 01:22:34.270
Anything happens, I'll be there.

01:22:35.980 --> 01:22:38.610
Thank you for all you've done.

01:22:40.610 --> 01:22:43.440
It was an honor to have met you.

01:22:45.030 --> 01:22:47.070
I'm grateful to you two.

01:22:48.240 --> 01:22:55.660
British Consulate-General

01:22:52.410 --> 01:22:55.080
Thank you for coming from Tokyo.

01:22:57.870 --> 01:23:00.840
British Consulate General

01:22:57.870 --> 01:23:00.840
Consulate

01:22:57.870 --> 01:23:00.840
General

01:22:57.870 --> 01:23:00.840
Nanba Branch Temple

01:22:57.870 --> 01:23:00.840
Main Hall

01:23:21.150 --> 01:23:22.480
Purse snatcher!

01:23:22.480 --> 01:23:25.110
Catch the guy on the bike!

01:23:25.820 --> 01:23:27.240
Are you alright?

01:23:29.950 --> 01:23:31.870
You, you're...

01:23:35.500 --> 01:23:36.580
Mr. Touma!

01:23:43.550 --> 01:23:45.840
There he is! He's in disguise!

01:23:47.260 --> 01:23:48.420
Don't shoot!

01:23:48.420 --> 01:23:51.800
We don't have permission to open fire here!

01:24:01.900 --> 01:24:02.770
Got him!

01:24:04.190 --> 01:24:05.480
What the hell?!

01:24:06.820 --> 01:24:08.030
Back off, fool!

01:24:08.190 --> 01:24:09.990
What's your problem?!

01:24:24.880 --> 01:24:26.000
Ms. Kasahara!

01:24:26.340 --> 01:24:27.880
Follow me, sir!

01:24:42.690 --> 01:24:43.860
Don't move!

01:24:44.650 --> 01:24:46.190
Don't try to resist!

01:24:59.040 --> 01:25:01.410
This is the Kanto LDF!

01:25:01.410 --> 01:25:03.710
Under the Library Law and

01:25:04.130 --> 01:25:06.540
my power as a Class 1 Librarian,

01:25:07.090 --> 01:25:09.210
we're taking Mr. Touma in!

01:25:10.050 --> 01:25:12.840
Actually, we're mostly Kansai LDF.

01:25:12.840 --> 01:25:14.470
Move!

01:25:23.060 --> 01:25:26.270
We'll handle these guys! Go, Kasahara!

01:25:36.660 --> 01:25:40.120
To my dear sister Asako, happy birthday!

01:25:40.500 --> 01:25:45.210
I'm in Gifu right now on a drive with Dad.

01:25:46.630 --> 01:25:52.170
Tomorrow we'll go shopping along Midosuji in Osaka.

01:25:52.170 --> 01:25:56.930
If we don't buy anything there, we'll head to Kita Ward.

01:25:57.680 --> 01:26:00.720
The US Consulate's there.

01:26:01.020 --> 01:26:02.890
Britain's is in Midosuji.

01:26:03.560 --> 01:26:05.140
Good thinking.

01:26:05.480 --> 01:26:10.980
So how come Captain Genda is going and I'm left holding the fort?

01:26:12.690 --> 01:26:14.780
We go to the US Consulate!

01:26:14.780 --> 01:26:16.160
Got it!

01:26:40.140 --> 01:26:42.310
Target is in Nakanoshima!

01:26:42.310 --> 01:26:43.310
Roger!

01:26:58.110 --> 01:27:00.450
Target is bound for Kita Ward!

01:27:01.870 --> 01:27:06.210
Directive from the MBC! Use of firearms is permitted!

01:27:06.210 --> 01:27:09.750
I repeat, use of firearms is permitted!

01:27:09.750 --> 01:27:11.630
Hold on, sir!

01:27:35.860 --> 01:27:37.860
This route is incorrect.

01:27:37.860 --> 01:27:40.530
Drive 300 meters and turn right.

01:27:40.530 --> 01:27:42.410
It's close! Let's go!

01:27:42.410 --> 01:27:43.200
Okay!

01:28:11.770 --> 01:28:14.980
Aim low! Mr. Touma's on board!

01:29:08.330 --> 01:29:10.120
I made a promise!

01:29:47.030 --> 01:29:48.160
Not yet!

01:29:48.660 --> 01:29:51.660
It's not over yet!

01:30:17.440 --> 01:30:19.320
You're on British soil!

01:30:21.360 --> 01:30:25.280
I suppose the Queen gave you entry passes?

01:30:30.830 --> 01:30:32.700
A diplomatic vehicle?!

01:30:34.290 --> 01:30:36.500
I'm with the Consulate.

01:30:36.500 --> 01:30:39.880
The LDF told us to look out for you.

01:30:39.880 --> 01:30:42.420
I request asylum in your country.

01:30:59.270 --> 01:31:01.230
Mission accomplished.

01:31:03.190 --> 01:31:06.360
I did it, Instructor.

01:31:24.800 --> 01:31:32.600
After Mr. Touma's defection, other nations have begun to condemn Japan's Media Betterment Act.

01:31:32.930 --> 01:31:39.650
In response, top officials are considering the necessity of a review of the law.

01:31:40.940 --> 01:31:46.150
I kind of expected things to change more dramatically.

01:31:46.530 --> 01:31:49.110
Oh come on! They will.

01:31:49.530 --> 01:31:50.780
Really?

01:31:50.780 --> 01:31:55.620
Japan's weak against foreign pressure, so things will improve.

01:31:56.080 --> 01:32:00.750
Then it's up to the efforts of anti-censorship lawmakers.

01:32:00.750 --> 01:32:04.500
Aha. I wonder if Tezuka's brother will be okay?

01:32:04.800 --> 01:32:09.590
If we can't rely on his character, we can trust his panache.

01:32:09.590 --> 01:32:13.970
He won't want to make history in an unsightly way.

01:32:16.890 --> 01:32:21.100
For the shame it's brought Japan, the Act is dying.

01:32:21.690 --> 01:32:26.030
If its power is diminished, the LDF will follow suit.

01:32:26.900 --> 01:32:28.860
The LDF will break up?!

01:32:28.860 --> 01:32:30.660
Not for a long time!

01:32:31.030 --> 01:32:37.120
By that time, even you'll be a senior librarian, so no need to worry.

01:32:39.120 --> 01:32:41.000
That'd be nice.

01:32:41.880 --> 01:32:46.050
Never mind that, when are you going to see Dojo?

01:32:54.470 --> 01:32:56.470
It's hard for me to go.

01:32:58.140 --> 01:33:03.060
He's getting grumpier by the day, so you'd better go soon.

01:33:03.480 --> 01:33:07.150
Tomorrow... I'll go tomorrow.

01:33:15.660 --> 01:33:20.870
I feel like I'm losing something by letting you go now.

01:33:21.410 --> 01:33:24.380
You mean that as Future Plan leader?

01:33:25.170 --> 01:33:29.380
You're welcome to regard it as my personal feeling.

01:33:31.510 --> 01:33:32.680
Knock it off!

01:33:32.680 --> 01:33:33.590
Hikaru?

01:33:33.720 --> 01:33:36.550
She's mine! Back off!

01:33:41.980 --> 01:33:44.690
I'll yield to your declaration.

01:33:46.360 --> 01:33:49.280
Looking forward to your next report.

01:33:51.650 --> 01:33:55.070
"Next report"?! What a nerve!

01:33:56.120 --> 01:33:57.450
Hey, Tezuka!

01:33:57.450 --> 01:33:58.330
Yes ma'am?!

01:33:58.330 --> 01:34:00.620
That was quite an outburst.

01:34:00.620 --> 01:34:02.910
I'm your... what exactly?

01:34:03.540 --> 01:34:07.250
Well, you're my... My...

01:34:07.750 --> 01:34:10.760
My colleague, I guess!

01:34:11.090 --> 01:34:12.420
Oh, really.

01:34:13.760 --> 01:34:14.970
Coward.

01:34:14.970 --> 01:34:16.180
What was that?

01:34:16.180 --> 01:34:20.100
It doesn't matter! Come on, let's head back!

01:34:20.810 --> 01:34:23.770
EAST SHINJUKU GENERAL HOSPITAL

01:34:26.060 --> 01:34:27.440
Ms. Kasahara!

01:34:31.900 --> 01:34:36.610
When I started working at the bookstore, the MBC raided it,

01:34:37.320 --> 01:34:39.490
and that's when I met Dojo.

01:34:50.130 --> 01:34:54.470
Later I asked him to date me, but he turned me down.

01:34:54.470 --> 01:34:56.930
"I'm not ready yet," he said.

01:34:56.930 --> 01:34:58.890
But, I...

01:34:59.390 --> 01:35:03.350
It's okay. I made up my mind to be on your side.

01:35:05.440 --> 01:35:08.900
Instructor Dojo is kind to me because

01:35:08.900 --> 01:35:11.980
he recognizes the effort I've put in.

01:35:14.490 --> 01:35:16.860
Your cute eyeglass case.

01:35:18.240 --> 01:35:22.200
That's not a reward for a hardworking colleague.

01:35:24.750 --> 01:35:27.670
It'll work out for you.

01:35:41.180 --> 01:35:43.850
Uh, um... Instructor Dojo?

01:35:43.850 --> 01:35:44.430
It's about time!

01:35:44.430 --> 01:35:45.810
I'm sorry!

01:35:46.430 --> 01:35:51.230
I completed my mission and returned one week ago, sir!

01:35:52.940 --> 01:35:53.530
Sit.

01:36:00.410 --> 01:36:04.580
Mr. Touma called the base, and he sounded well.

01:36:04.580 --> 01:36:05.580
That's good.

01:36:08.000 --> 01:36:12.000
If you're angry, let's get this over with quickly!

01:36:12.000 --> 01:36:14.590
I told you! You're late!

01:36:14.590 --> 01:36:17.170
Well, it's complicated.

01:36:17.840 --> 01:36:22.300
See my leg? You don't come, you don't get commended.

01:36:27.480 --> 01:36:29.600
Komaki told me everything.

01:36:30.940 --> 01:36:32.690
You really did great.

01:36:38.240 --> 01:36:42.570
If you mean it, please don't look so angry!

01:36:53.420 --> 01:36:54.920
Oh, Instructor!

01:36:55.550 --> 01:36:56.590
Here!

01:36:58.300 --> 01:37:01.720
You promised to tell me something, remember?

01:37:02.090 --> 01:37:05.850
Thanks to you, I survived. I kept my promise.

01:37:07.100 --> 01:37:09.810
This is as good as me saying it!

01:37:11.060 --> 01:37:12.770
I kept my promise.

01:37:15.940 --> 01:37:18.110
If I say it, what happens?

01:37:18.110 --> 01:37:20.200
I have to hear it first.

01:37:25.490 --> 01:37:26.660
I love you.

01:37:27.790 --> 01:37:33.960
The fact that you've been
my prince since I was in high school

01:37:34.210 --> 01:37:36.000
doesn't matter anymore.

01:37:36.500 --> 01:37:38.630
I love the man you are now!

01:37:38.630 --> 01:37:39.840
Enough of that.

01:37:39.840 --> 01:37:41.300
It's not enough!

01:37:41.760 --> 01:37:45.350
I love who you are now!

01:37:45.970 --> 01:37:49.680
You became the man you are today eight years since then.

01:37:50.310 --> 01:37:51.430
I...

01:37:52.190 --> 01:37:54.350
I love who you are now!

01:37:54.940 --> 01:37:57.400
That's enough! Don't say that!

01:37:57.730 --> 01:38:01.740
It's not enough! You told me to say all this!

01:38:01.740 --> 01:38:02.530
I...

01:38:09.240 --> 01:38:13.160
I'm sorry. I understand. I won't say any more.

01:38:13.830 --> 01:38:17.460
Wait, you don't understand! Not at all!

01:38:17.920 --> 01:38:19.090
But...

01:38:19.090 --> 01:38:20.670
Just sit down.

01:38:22.300 --> 01:38:26.640
I meant, don't say that stuff about me being a prince.

01:38:49.950 --> 01:38:53.500
The Bluebird Knights
Touma Kurato

01:39:02.420 --> 01:39:09.890
Books

01:39:02.420 --> 01:39:09.890
Forces

01:39:05.260 --> 01:39:09.890
If I'd joined up earlier, I could've fired live rounds.

01:39:09.890 --> 01:39:11.600
Too bad.

01:39:11.600 --> 01:39:16.850
The Act was revised last year to prohibit the use of firearms.

01:39:17.190 --> 01:39:20.190
Wish I could've shot a Sig Sauer!

01:39:20.190 --> 01:39:22.230
Hey dumb asses!

01:39:24.400 --> 01:39:25.820
Instructor Dojo!

01:39:26.280 --> 01:39:32.290
You know how tough it was before guns were banned from the censorship war?

01:39:32.410 --> 01:39:34.540
Drop and give me twenty!

01:39:34.790 --> 01:39:40.540
Passing through the soundly asleep residential district

01:39:34.790 --> 01:39:40.540
neikitateru juutakugai wo nukete

01:39:41.670 --> 01:39:47.380
in a hurry to meet you soon

01:39:41.670 --> 01:39:47.380
kimi ni sukoshi ai ni isoi da

01:39:48.050 --> 01:39:53.850
The city's night sky also cheering me on

01:39:48.050 --> 01:39:53.850
machi no yozora mo ganbatte kureteru

01:39:54.720 --> 01:40:01.560
It's as though my heart was possessed by my teenage self

01:39:54.720 --> 01:40:01.560
mune ni juudai no jibun ga toritsuite shimatta mitai da

01:40:02.150 --> 01:40:07.320
Without you = All alone, somehow

01:40:02.150 --> 01:40:07.320
kimi ga inai ikuoru hitoribocchi nante sa

01:40:08.820 --> 01:40:17.080
I hate my lonely self to the extent of wanting to swallow it at once

01:40:08.820 --> 01:40:17.080
kiratte hodo kodoku wo nomihoshi ta boku na noni

01:40:17.080 --> 01:40:20.630
It has begun

01:40:17.080 --> 01:40:20.630
hajimatte shimatterunda

